# ── Not for the public repo ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Manuscript. Lives with the paper, not the code.
paper_draft/
paper_study2_pipeline_draft.md

# Working session artefacts: plans that were superseded or never implemented,
# and the dated handover. The repo ships the pipeline, not the record of
# building it. README.md, WORKFLOW.md, COMMANDS.md and CHANGELOG.md stay.
PLAN_Study2.md
PLAN_fixes_2026-08-20.md
PLAN_query_layer.md
PLAN_texture_quality.md
HANDOVER.md

# Dated validation notes. The protocols and results they document belong with
# the paper; the released ground truth itself (05_output/test_set_labels*.csv,
# 01_input/test_tiles*) stays in the repo so the evaluation is reproducible.
06_validation/

# Scratch crops from the exemplar searches. Regenerable, and not part of the
# released set: the ground truth is 01_input/test_tiles*/ and
# 05_output/test_set_labels*.csv.
05_output/rust_candidates/
05_output/rust_candidates2/
05_output/efflorescence_candidates/

# build_reference_set.py writes candidates here for hand-picking. The loader
# ignores underscore folders, and these still carry retired label names.
01_input/reference_surfaces/_candidates/

# Regenerable caches and diagnostics
01_input/test_tiles*/_texel_density.json
05_output/binary_probe_misses.csv

COMMIT_MESSAGE.txt

# ── Full-resolution meshes: archived on Zenodo, not in git ─────────────────
# 2.7 GB of LFS content against GitHub's 1 GB free quota, and the same meshes
# were stored twice (01_input and 05_output). The repo keeps the records, the
# ground truth and the web-sized models in docs/. See README, "Full-resolution
# meshes", for the DOI.
01_input/meshes/processed/*/*.glb
01_input/meshes/processed/*/*_texture.png
05_output/descriptors/*.glb
05_output/descriptors/*_texture.png

# Working backups from the FS-001 re-bake
*pre-retarget*
